    <Byline publishedDate="2026-03-16" />

    <div class="bg-secondary/40 border-l-4 border-primary rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4 mb-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground mb-1">Direct Answer</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">At 6'7" and above, mainstream ergonomic chairs are at their limits. The Steelcase Leap Plus comes closest, at 19.75" of seat depth and up to 22.5" of seat height with the optional 5" cylinder — mandatory at this height, since the standard cylinder stops at 19.5". It also has a real return window — which makes it the sensible first test rather than the guaranteed answer. If after correct setup the seat still cannot reach your popliteal height, or thigh pressure persists, that is concrete evidence for commercial-grade or custom seating.</p>
